  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "The graph passes through $(-1,0)$, $(3,0)$, and $(0,-3)$. Find its equation. (Let the equation be $y=ax^2+bx+c$. Give $a$, $b$, and $c$ in that order, separated by commas.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "1，-2，-3",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "From $(0,-3)$, we obtain $c=-3$. Substituting the other 2 points gives $a-b-3=0$ and $9a+3b-3=0$. Solving gives $a=1$ and $b=-2$, so $y=x^2-2x-3$.\n\nAlternative method 1: Use the two zeros\n\nThe two points with \\(y=0\\) give the zeros \\(-1\\) and \\(3\\), so use the quadratic intercept form\n\\[\ny=a(x+1)(x-3),\\qquad a\\ne0.\n\\]\nThis builds in both zeros and leaves only one coefficient to find. Substituting \\((0,-3)\\) gives \\(-3=-3a\\), hence \\(a=1\\). Expanding gives \\(y=x^2-2x-3\\), so the requested coefficients are \\(1,-2,-3\\).",
